.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:11:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:12:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:13:# Worktree may have files in the index but absent from the working tree filesystem
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:15:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:16:During T10 dispatch the manager observed that the worktree at `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/268-session-foundations-bundle-b/` had 953 files showing in `git status --short` as ` D` (working-tree deleted, index retained). The Edit and Read tools failed against those paths because the physical files were missing, yet `git -C <worktree> show HEAD:<path>` succeeded — proving the tracked version existed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:18:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:19:Adopt a pre-flight worktree-integrity check before any executor or assistant editing pass against the worktree:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:20:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:21:PHYS=$(git -C <worktree> status --short | grep -c "^ D")
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:22:if [ "$PHYS" -gt 0 ]; then
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:23:  git -C <worktree> checkout HEAD -- .
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:24:fi
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:25:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:26:The restore is safe because the index is the source of truth for the branch's intended content.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:28:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:29:- Failing Read/Edit calls inside an executor produce confusing errors that look like missing files rather than worktree-state drift.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:30:- The remediation is a single `git checkout HEAD -- <path>` (or `-- .` for bulk); without the pre-flight check executors burn time on misdiagnosis.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:32:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:33:- Recreate the worktree from scratch. Rejected — destroys per-iter commits that may not be pushed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:34:- Trust the executor to detect the missing files. Rejected — Read tool failures look like missing-file errors, not worktree drift.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:36:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:37:- Delegation prompts targeting worktree files should include the pre-flight check or a "restore-if-needed" note.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:38:- Wrap-up's own routing pass may need to run the same pre-flight if it ever writes to worktree-internal paths (this session it only writes to main-tree `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/` so does not).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:40:## How to recognize next time
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:41:- Bash `ls <worktree>/.gobbi/projects/...` returns "No such file or directory" but `git -C <worktree> ls-files <path>` returns the path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:42:- `git -C <worktree> status --short | head` shows many ` D` (space-D) entries.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:44:## Corrected approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:45:- Pre-flight: `git -C <worktree> status --short | grep -c "^ D"` — if > 0, run `git -C <worktree> checkout HEAD -- <path>`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:46:- For Wrap-up: prefer the main-tree `.gobbi/projects/{project}/` for all project-memory writes (already the canonical location).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:48:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:49:- T1 implementation (PR #269) — worktree-first session architecture
