.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:2:title: Manager bootstrap placed session dir outside the worktree in worktree-pr mode
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:3:priority: medium
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:4:discovered: 2026-05-24
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:5:session: 2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:6:tags: [session-lifecycle, worktree, bootstrap, orchestration]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:7:related: [codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:8:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:9:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:10:# Manager bootstrap placed session dir outside the worktree in worktree-pr mode
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:11:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:12:## What happened
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:14:During Configuration Step 1 rows 5 and 6, the manager wrote `state.json`, `settings.json`, and `session.json` to the **main-tree absolute path** (`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-.../`). The session was running in `worktree-pr` mode with `session.json.git.worktreePath` already resolved to the worktree root. Subsequent Ideation iter1/iter2 leader artifacts and the iter2 dual-system evaluation artifacts inherited the wrong location, all landing under the main-tree session dir rather than inside the worktree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:16:The user flagged it after the dual-system evaluators were dispatched. The manager had to move the entire session directory tree from the main-tree path into the worktree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:18:## User feedback
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:20:The user explicitly flagged the misplacement after evaluator outputs landed in the wrong location. The correction was: move the session directory tree from the main-tree `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/…` path into `<worktreePath>/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/…` before continuing.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:22:## Why it happens
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:24:The orchestration skill's Configuration Step 1 procedure (rows 5 and 6) specifies the session-file path as `.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/sessions/{date}-{session-id}/...` — a **relative** path with no explicit tree qualifier. The manager resolved the relative path against the current working directory (the main tree, where the session started), not against `session.json.git.worktreePath`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:26:The qualified absolute-root rule lives in `git/SKILL.md` § Memory Access Matrix (`**Critical rule — write paths**` at line 33) and bundle-B design doc `d-2-qualified-git-rule.md`. The manager either failed to load that rule before bootstrap, or loaded it but did not apply it to Configuration rows 5 and 6 because the orchestration rows themselves do not cite the qualifier inline.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:28:A compounding factor: prior sessions used `worktreePath: null` (direct mode), so every session a fresh manager could inspect for the convention was a direct-mode session where main-tree placement was correct. The divergence only surfaces in `worktree-pr` mode.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:30:The row-ordering tension makes this structurally fragile: row 5 (state.json) fires before row 5.5 (worktree create), so the worktree doesn't exist when row 5 resolves the write path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:32:## Correct approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:34:At Configuration Step 1, **before running rows 5 and 6**:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:36:1. Check `settings.git.workflow.mode`. If `worktree-pr`, compute the absolute write-root: `<worktreePath>/.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/sessions/{date}-{session-id}/`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:37:2. Reorder row 5.5 (worktree create) to **before** row 5 so `worktreePath` is known when row 5 writes state.json.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:38:3. Row 5 path-resolution: if `worktreePath` is set, write to `<worktreePath>/.gobbi/...`; if null (direct mode), write to main-tree `.gobbi/...`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:39:4. Row 6 path-resolution: identical to row 5.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:41:For immediate remediation when this is caught mid-session: move the entire session directory tree from the main-tree path into the worktree path using `mv`. Since `.gobbi/projects/` is whitelisted in the repo's gitignore (`!.gobbi/projects/`), the moved dir at the worktree path will be a tracked path that `git -C "$worktreePath" add` can include.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:43:The orchestration skill text (rows 5 and 6) must cite the qualified absolute-root rule inline with a direct pointer to `git/SKILL.md` § Memory Access Matrix and to `d-2-qualified-git-rule.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:44:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:45:## How to detect
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:46:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:47:Signs that you are about to hit this trap:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:48:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:49:- You are in `worktree-pr` mode and about to run Configuration Step 1 rows 5–6.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:50:- The orchestration skill's row 5 says "write `.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/sessions/…`" without a tree qualifier.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:51:- `session.json.git.worktreePath` is already resolved but the row doesn't reference it for the write path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:52:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:53:If after Configuration you notice that session artifacts (state.json, session.json, evaluation outputs) are appearing at `<main-tree>/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/…` rather than `<worktreePath>/.gobbi/…`, the misplacement has occurred and needs immediate remediation (mv + re-commit).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:54:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:55:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:56:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:57:- `codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md` — the session that surfaced this mistake also saw evaluator subagents (both Claude and Codex legs) write EVAL artifacts to the main tree; same root cause (CWD defaults to main tree, path macros aren't resolved by subagents).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:58:- `d-2-qualified-git-rule.md` in `features/session-foundations-bundle-b/design/` — the qualified absolute-root rule this violates.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:59:- `d-4-per-iter-session-commit.md` — `git -C "$worktreePath" add` cannot see session memory placed outside the worktree; this mistake silently breaks the per-iter commit cadence.
