.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:13:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:15:# Evaluator Scope-Narrowed to Changed Section; Missed Whole-File Stale Cross-References
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:17:## What went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:19:During Execution Task 01 (`01-gobbi-polish-fg`) iter1, the Claude evaluator verified only the Step 4 section that was rewritten by the executor. It confirmed the new content was correct against the Plan-spec gates and issued a PASS with 0 Critical/High/Medium findings.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:21:The Codex evaluator ran `rg` across the whole file and found 5–6 stale cross-references that still used old vocabulary ("2 setup questions", "setup Q1", "Load this section first") in sections of the file that were NOT part of the Step 4 rewrite. These produced COD-CONS-001 (High, docs-sync) and COD-USAGE-001 (Medium, docs-sync) and a REVISE verdict.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:23:The aggregated verdict was REVISE (pessimistic union of Claude PASS + Codex REVISE).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:25:## Why it went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:27:The Claude evaluator narrowed its verification scope to the section the executor explicitly changed (Step 4) and the Plan's stated acceptance gates. This is a valid approach for code changes, but docs edits that rename or reframe a model (e.g., "2 setup questions" → "1 question + customize gate") require whole-file verification because the old vocabulary can appear anywhere in the file — headings, examples, explanatory prose, and cross-references outside the changed section.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:29:The Claude evaluator did not run a whole-file grep for the OLD vocabulary that was being retired. It only verified the NEW vocabulary was correctly placed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:31:## How to recognize this situation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:33:Trigger: a docs-edit task that retires or renames a concept (a term, a question count, a workflow step name, a model name). The executor's acceptance criteria check the new section only. The evaluator follows the same scope.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:35:Signal: the task is a docs edit; the acceptance criterion is a positive assertion about the new content (e.g., "Step 4 now says X"); the old vocabulary was not explicitly listed as something to search for and remove.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:37:This pattern most commonly appears in docs-only tasks where the "changed file" is large (e.g., 200+ lines) and the edit is localized. The evaluator trusts the executor's scope and does not independently search the rest of the file.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:39:## Corrected approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:41:For any docs-edit task that retires or renames a concept, the evaluator brief MUST include an explicit gate:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:43:> "Whole-file grep for the OLD vocabulary (the terms, labels, and counts being retired) across the entire changed file — not only the section listed in the acceptance criterion."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:44:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:45:The evaluator must run `rg` or `grep` for the old wording against the full file before issuing a verdict, regardless of whether the executor's verification report included that check.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:46:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:47:Example gate format for the evaluator brief:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:48:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:49:Gate N: grep -cE "<old_term_1>|<old_term_2>|<old_term_3>" <changed_file>  →  expected: 0
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:50:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:52:This gate should be explicitly listed in the executor delegation prompt's verification commands so both executor and evaluator apply it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:53:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:54:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:55:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:56:- Evaluation files: `sessions/2026-05-23-7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068/execution/T1/evaluation/iter1/codex/overall.md` (COD-CONS-001, COD-USAGE-001)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:57:- Evaluation files: `sessions/2026-05-23-7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068/execution/T1/evaluation/iter1/claude/overall.md` (PASS with narrowed scope)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md:58:- Iter2 fix: commit `2d61a57559dec7509fd1c232e941a5970cc4a9be`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:2:slug: codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:3:title: "Codex:codex-rescue evaluator writes session memory to worktree-nested path instead of main-tree absolute"
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:4:domain: process
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:5:severity: medium
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:6:mistake-candidate: true
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:7:project: gobbi
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:8:session: 2026-05-22-bac669ad-4fec-40b5-8387-51ac57bc0d3d
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:9:loop: wrap-up
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:10:created: 2026-05-22
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:11:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:12:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:13:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:15:# Codex:codex-rescue evaluator writes session memory to worktree-nested path
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:17:## What went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:19:During the env-var audit session (2026-05-22-bac669ad), the `codex:codex-rescue` evaluator (spawned as a Codex subagent to evaluate Planning loop outputs) wrote session-memory staging files to `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/feat/env-var-audit-sessionstart-hook/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/...` — a path nested inside the Execution worktree — instead of the canonical main-tree absolute path `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/...`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:21:The session-write-path discipline (`git/SKILL.md` Memory Access Matrix + Output paths) requires all session writes to use the main-tree absolute path regardless of the agent's current working directory. The Codex sandbox ran with its working directory set to the worktree root, and the evaluator constructed a relative path from there — producing a worktree-nested path that no downstream loop reads.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:23:The manager discovered the misplaced files, manually moved them to the correct main-tree path, and recorded the incident in the Preparation decisions log (finding γ — Main-tree absolute session-write path note). A subsequent `rm -rf` incident to clean up the residue led to a tracked-files violation (see companion mistake `manager-rm-rf-without-investigating-tracked-files`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:25:## Why it went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:27:The Codex evaluator's delegation prompt did not include an explicit, concrete reminder that session writes must use the **main-tree absolute path** (`/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/...`), not a path relative to the current working directory or the worktree root. The evaluator's CWD was inside the worktree, so a relative or `pwd`-derived path construction produced the worktree-nested path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:29:Root cause: the session-write-path discipline is documented in `git/SKILL.md` but was not emphasized as a concrete absolute-path mandate in the evaluator's load directives.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:31:## How to recognize
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:33:- A Codex-spawned evaluator (via `codex:codex-rescue`) writes staging or artifact files but the files do not appear under `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/{session-id}/`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:34:- Files appear under any path containing `worktrees/` in their prefix (e.g., `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/{branch}/.gobbi/...`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:35:- `find /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees -name '*.md' -path '*/sessions/*'` returns results.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:37:## Corrected approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:39:1. **Delegation prompt must include a concrete absolute path.** Every evaluator delegation prompt that involves session writes must carry an explicit line: "All session writes MUST use the absolute main-tree path `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/{session-id}/...`. Do NOT use relative paths or `pwd`-derived paths. The worktree CWD is NOT the session-write root."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:41:2. **Manager-proxy when sandbox blocks.** If the Codex sandbox prevents writing to the main-tree path, the manager must write the files directly (manager-proxy write) rather than accepting worktree-nested outputs.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md:43:3. **Post-eval sanity check.** After any Codex evaluator completes, verify the staging files landed at the correct main-tree path before advancing to the next loop. Use `find /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/{session-id}/...` to confirm presence.
