.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:15:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:17:# Mistake Candidate: Edit Tool Refuses Symlink Paths — Use Canonical Path
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:19:## What went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:21:During Task 01 Execution, the executor attempted to edit `.claude/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` (a symlink) using the Edit tool. The tool refused with "Refusing to write through symlink". The executor fell back to the canonical target path `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` and the edit succeeded.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:23:The Preparation iter3 edit contract states "Edit tool default = safe via either path" — this claim is empirically FALSE in this Claude Code environment.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:25:## Why it went wrong (mistaken assumption)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:27:The edit contract assumed the Edit tool would follow symlinks transparently. It does not — it refuses to write through symlink paths. The canonical path (the actual target of the symlink) is the correct path for Edit operations.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:29:## How to recognize
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:31:Trigger signals:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:32:- Edit tool returns "Refusing to write through symlink" when targeting a path under `.claude/skills/`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:33:- The task involves editing a skill file via its `.claude/` mirror path rather than the canonical `.gobbi/projects/.../skills/` path
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:34:- The edit contract is being followed and names `.claude/` path as the safe default
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:36:## Corrected approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:38:Always use the canonical mirror path (`.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/skills/{skill-path}`) for Edit tool operations on skill files, not the symlink path (`.claude/skills/{skill-path}`). The symlink remains valid for reads; only Edit/Write require the canonical path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:40:Specific correction for the edit contract doc: amend point 1 of the safety table to read: "Edit tool may refuse symlink paths; canonical path (`.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/skills/...`) is the always-safe fallback."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:42:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:44:- `execution/task-01/evaluation/iter1/claude/overall.md` — finding O-001
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/edit-tool-refuses-symlink-paths.md:45:- Preparation iter3 edit contract (safety-table point 1) — the doc that needs updating
