.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:20:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:22:# Evaluator returns verdict inline; no per-perspective files written
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:24:## What went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:26:T05 Claude evaluator (iter1) returned a PASS verdict with full per-perspective findings inline in its response. It did NOT write the contracted 8 per-perspective .md files (project / structure / performance / aesthetics / usage / consistency / risk / overall) to the evaluation output dir despite the brief explicitly requiring those output paths.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:28:Manager wrote a proxy overall.md to preserve the verdict and 2 Low findings to disk for audit-trail continuity, but project / structure / performance / aesthetics / usage / consistency / risk per-perspective files are missing from `sessions/.../execution/T5/evaluation/iter1/claude/`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:30:## Why it went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:32:The `evaluator` agent type's `tools` list per `.claude/agents/evaluator.md` is `Read, Grep, Glob, Bash` — **no `Write` tool**. The evaluator interpreted this absence (plus possibly some directive in the agent system prompt to "not write report .md files") as forbidding file writes, and chose to return findings inline.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:34:This is BOTH a tools issue (no Write means writes must go via Bash heredoc) AND a behavioral issue (the evaluator chose inline rather than `cat > file.md << EOF` via Bash). Prior evaluators in this session DID write files (via Bash heredoc); this one chose differently.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:36:## How to recognize
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:38:- Evaluator's response begins with verdict + findings TABLE in the chat
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:39:- `ls sessions/.../evaluation/iter{N}/{system}/` shows fewer than 8 files (or only `overall.md`)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:40:- Evaluator self-narrates a directive conflict like "I should NOT write report .md files, but the brief requires per-perspective files... I'll return inline."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:42:## Corrected approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:44:Either:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:46:1. **Add `Write` to evaluator's `tools` list** (in `.claude/agents/evaluator.md`) so file writes are first-class. The evaluator brief already specifies output paths; the role's tool surface should match.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:48:2. **Make Bash-heredoc-write explicit in the evaluator brief**. Add a line: "If you lack the Write tool, use `mkdir -p <dir> && cat > <path> << 'EOF' ... EOF` via Bash for each of the 8 per-perspective files. Do NOT return findings inline — the per-perspective files are the audit trail."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:49:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:50:3. **Add a verification gate to the manager's post-evaluation step**: after evaluator returns DONE, manager runs `ls -1 sessions/.../evaluation/iter{N}/{system}/ | wc -l` — must return 8. If not, re-dispatch the evaluator with explicit Bash-write instructions.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:52:Recommended: combine (2) into the evaluator brief template at `.claude/skills/delegation/templates/evaluator.md` AND (3) as a manager-side check.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:53:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:54:## Witness
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:55:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:56:- T05 iter1 Claude eval: agent ID `a0bf7024f118377d1` returned verdict + inline findings; `ls execution/T5/evaluation/iter1/claude/` after dispatch showed 0 files (manager later wrote proxy overall.md).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:57:- Comparison: prior evaluators in this session (Ideation iter1-3, Preparation iter1-3, Planning iter1-2, Execution T1-T4) all wrote 8 per-perspective files via Bash heredoc.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/evaluator-returned-verdict-inline-no-per-perspective-files.md:58:- Tool surface verification: `grep "^tools:" .claude/agents/evaluator.md` → `tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash` (no Write).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:2:date: 2026-05-24
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:3:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:4:status: accepted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:5:feature: session-foundations-bundle-b
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:6:loop: planning
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:7:mistake-candidate: true
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:8:domain: process
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:9:finding-id: codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:10:type: general
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:11:disposition: open
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:12:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:13:superseded_by: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:16:# Codex wrapper used relative paths — wrote to wrong session directory
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:18:## What went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:20:Codex assistant-wrapper for Planning iter2 evaluation was composed with relative ellipsis paths (e.g., `sessions/.../planning/...`) rather than absolute paths. Codex's sandbox CWD resolved these paths against a different session directory from yesterday's session (`2026-05-23-7ea62d36-...`). The wrapper wrote nothing to the correct current-session directory but validated against stale files from that prior session and reported PASS — a false PASS against wrong files.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:22:## Why it went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:24:The wrapper assumed Codex would inherit the parent session's working context (specifically the session ID and the base path). It omitted absolute path discipline in the prompt. Relative paths in Codex invocations are CWD-resolved, and CWD is the Codex sandbox root, not the gobbi session directory. This created a silent path mismatch with no error output, producing a confident but wrong PASS.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:26:## How to recognize
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:28:- Codex output files are timestamped before the current session's start time.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:29:- Codex evaluation findings reference content from a different session (e.g., mentioning features or decisions from yesterday's session that are not in the current iter's draft).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:30:- Codex per-perspective files appear in the wrong session directory path (prior session ID in the path).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:31:- Codex reports PASS on a plan that has known High findings which were not resolved.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:32:- The `.codex-marker` file (written as a first action) is absent in the expected current-session directory but present in a prior-session directory.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:34:## Corrected approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:36:1. Every path passed to Codex MUST be absolute. Never use relative paths, never use `...` ellipsis shorthand in path arguments.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:37:2. Wrapper writes a `.wrapper-marker` file with the current timestamp AND current session ID to the correct target directory BEFORE Codex invocation. Instructions to Codex: verify `.wrapper-marker` exists and write `.codex-marker` alongside it as the first action — this proves Codex is operating in the right directory.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:38:3. Wrapper validate-step after Codex completion: list the absolute target directory; grep for current-iter draft reference in the output files; verify `.codex-marker` exists at the absolute path. If any check fails, the wrapper treats the run as void and re-dispatches.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:39:4. Pattern proven in the retry that produced the correct Planning iter2 PASS: absolute paths + marker verification + validate-step.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:41:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:43:- Session `2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac` Planning iter2
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md:44:- The stale-session PASS was detected because Claude evaluator independently verified Codex's claimed empirical checks and found them to reference prior-session artifacts
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:1:---
