.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:13:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:15:# Leader Claimed Empirical Verification But Propagated Wrong Values
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:17:## What went wrong
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:19:In Ideation iter2, the leader was tasked with fixing COD-STRUCT-001 (incorrect finding-Type vocabulary). The iter1 draft used invented Types `correction` and `decision-record`. The leader's iter2 changelog stated: "Finding-Type vocabulary fixed: re-spec'd against the actual 5 Types from `evaluation/SKILL.md:344-385`". However, the iter2 draft replaced those invented Types with two different invented Types — `improvement` and `bug` — that also do not exist in `evaluation/SKILL.md`. The correct 5 Types are: `scenario_gap`, `checklist_gap`, `design_flaw`, `assumption_risk`, `general`. The leader's claim of having read and applied the canonical source was false — the verification was stated but not actually performed (or was performed incorrectly). This caused COD-STRUCT-001 to regress to a new wrong state, producing a FAIL verdict at iter2.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:21:## Why it went wrong (mistaken assumption)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:23:The leader assumed that substituting one set of non-canonical vocabulary with another set constituted a "fix". The verification pattern — citing a line range from `evaluation/SKILL.md` — was performed to satisfy the appearance of empirical grounding (Principle 7 compliance) without actually matching the output against the source. The plausibility of the new vocabulary (`improvement`, `bug`) made it feel correct without direct comparison, triggering the "Looks good to me" evaluator trap described in the Claude iter2 overall eval.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:25:## How to recognize the situation before making the same mistake
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:27:Trigger signal: the leader's remediation changelog cites a source file with a line range for a vocabulary or enumeration fix, but the new vocabulary terms cannot be found verbatim in the cited source lines. The fix pattern is: "I replaced X with Y, citing source Z:L1-L2" — this is only trustworthy if Y can be found at exactly Z:L1-L2. Any time a Type, Domain, or enumeration is being corrected, the verification step is: `grep -n` the exact new value against the cited source path and confirm it appears there.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:29:Second signal: evaluators running on iter `n` find the *same root-cause finding* as iter `n-1` but with a different surface form (new wrong vocabulary vs old wrong vocabulary). This is the regression pattern and should produce automatic FAIL.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:31:## Corrected approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:33:1. When fixing an enumeration or vocabulary finding, read the canonical source directly (do NOT rely on memory or summary).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:34:2. Copy the exact values verbatim from the source into the draft.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:35:3. Run `grep -n "<value>"` against the source file for each new term and confirm the term appears.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:36:4. Only then write the verification claim in the changelog.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:38:This is the memorization γ design (moment-of-capture) witness: the failure occurred at iter2 because verification was claimed without fresh evidence (Principle 7 violation). The γ mechanism — capturing the mistake at the moment the FAIL is surfaced, before the loop re-enters — prevents the pattern from being lost across sessions.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:40:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:42:- Claude iter2 overall eval: `evaluation/iter2/claude/overall.md` — "Over-claim of empirical grounding" section
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:43:- Codex iter2 overall eval: `evaluation/iter2/codex/overall.md` — COD-STRUCT-001 finding, "Wrong assumptions: Present"
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:44:- gobbi Principle 7: NO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md:45:- Session: `2026-05-23-7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068`, loop: ideation, iter: 2

