    37	The root cause was that no single rule captured "where does the write go when a
    38	worktree exists?" and "where does it go when one does not?"
    39	
    40	## Approach
    41	
    42	The v0.5.0 worktree-first model resolves the ambiguity with a single canonical
    43	decision made at Configuration Step 1 before any loop work begins.
    44	
    45	**Worktree creation precedes session.json init (D-1).** Row 5 of the
    46	Configuration Step 1 table in `orchestration/SKILL.md` creates the per-session
    47	worktree via `git/SKILL.md § P2` and holds the worktree path in-turn for use by
    48	rows 5.5 (state.json init) and 6 (session.json init). Row 6 stamps
    49	`session.json.git.worktreePath` and `session.json.git.branch`; from row 6 onward
    50	`session.json.git.worktreePath` is the canonical write-root. Branch naming follows
    51	the convention: `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` (e.g.,
    52	`chore/session-2026-05-24-45388fa9`), where `{ssid-short}` is the first 8
    53	characters of `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. The full branch name is 33 characters;
    54	the slug portion `session-YYYY-MM-DD-{8chars}` is 27 characters, which satisfies
    55	the `git/conventions.md` 3-50 character length constraint on description slugs.
    56	
    57	**`worktreePath` is the absolute write-root (D-2).** The qualified rule in
    58	`git/SKILL.md` Memory Access Matrix and Constraints reads: "Use
    59	`session.json.git.worktreePath` as the absolute root when set; fall back to the
    60	main tree absolute path when `worktreePath` is null (direct mode)." Transcript
    61	paths (`session.json.transcriptPath`) live in `~/.claude/projects/` — outside
    62	both trees — and are never redirected.
    63	
    64	**Per-iteration session-memory commit cadence (D-4).** After each MEMORIZATION
    65	sub-phase completes, the manager commits the iteration's session-memory deltas to
    66	the worktree branch via `git -C "$worktreePath" commit`. Subject:
    67	`chore(session): record {loop} iter{n} memory`. This ensures session memory
    68	survives mid-session abort before Wrap-up runs — `git worktree remove` (Procedure
    69	P5) discards uncommitted state; committed state survives.
    70	
    71	**Direct-mode opt-out retained (D-5).** Row 5 is guarded: when
    72	`settings.git.workflow.mode == "direct"`, the row is skipped entirely — no
    73	worktree is created, `session.json.git.worktreePath` stays `null`, and
    74	`git.branch` is stamped from the current HEAD in row 6. Direct mode is the
    75	documented escape hatch for emergency hotfixes (where the PR lifecycle overhead is
    76	unacceptable) and pure-read sessions (no shippable artifact). Outside these two
    77	situations the default is `worktree-pr`.
    78	
